  "statement": "Find the coefficient of $x^3$ in the expansion of $(1-2x)^{-2}$.",
  "solution": "$(1+u)^{-2}=\\sum\\binom{-2}{k}u^k$ with $u=-2x$. $\\binom{-2}{3}=\\dfrac{(-2)(-3)(-4)}{6}=-4$, and the $x^3$ term is $(-4)(-2x)^3=(-4)(-8)x^3=32x^3$. The coefficient is $32$.",
  "hints": [
    "Use the generalised binomial coefficient $\binom{-2}{3}$.",
    "Substitute $u=-2x$ and keep the $x^3$ term."
  ],
